{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg9vMUmwfDrZNG7TCKgju","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The path-separator check now covers every `--and` pattern, not just the main one. So `fd foo --and one/two` fails with the error `The search pattern 'one/two' contains a path-separation character…` instead of quietly returning no results.\n\n- **Change (`src/main.rs`):** the per-pattern check moved into a new helper, `ensure_pattern_is_not_a_path`. `ensure_search_pattern_is_not_a_path` now runs it on the main pattern and then on each `--and` pattern. The error names whichever pattern is at fault. `--full-path` still skips the check entirely.\n- **Test:** `test_and_pattern_with_forward_slash_is_rejected` in `tests/tests.rs`. It fails without the fix and passes with it, and the existing slash-pattern tests still pass. The format, whitespace and debug-leftover checks also passed.\n- **Not checked:** the Windows-only `\\` branch (only the variable names changed there), and I didn't run the full test suite."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":429,"cache_read_input_tokens":35216,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":429,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":328,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"39e2d230-c17a-4416-8dcc-ebb3fa0be4fa","uuid":"f5da1361-6d32-4036-99c0-6d47fdc2d7a6","timestamp":"2026-10-18T15:14:21.173Z","request_id":"req_011Cg9vMUaYRLbkja1ksjpus"}
